+## GLM expert prompt kernels from glm53f-afd (TF_GLM_EXPERT_KERNEL=g53)
+
+`families/glm5_next/cuda/g53_rank.cu` (with `g53_rank.h`, `g53_rank.cpp` and `g53_experts.py`) holds expert prompt
+kernels from glm53f-afd, written by Hugh Madden (@dangerm00se, [github.com/hughmadden](https://github.com/hughmadden)),
+[glm53f-afd @ 91db3cc](https://github.com/hughmadden/glm53f-afd/tree/91db3cc6fe672e2724efa3464f63bd31493f63f6):
+`crates/glm53f-rank/kernels/exl3_rank.cu`'s plan, its large-M gate/up and down kernels (`gateup_big`, `down_big`), its
+fused epilogue and reduce (`epilogue_item`, `reduce_item`, `gateup_tail`, `down_tail`), its unfused epilogue and reduce
+kernels and its persistent launch, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Turquoise Bay AI Pty Ltd (see
+[the license text](LICENSES/glm53f-afd-MIT.txt)). That file's EXL3 trellis decoder (`mcg2`, `decode_tile`), fragment
+MMA (`mma16816`) and Hadamard butterfly (`fwht128`) come from TensorFold by Ash Hart (@ashxhart,
+[github.com/ashhart](https://github.com/ashhart)), [TensorFold @ bb4b4a3](https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold/tree/bb4b4a3),
+MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 TensorFold contributors, kept with glm53f-afd's `LICENSE.tensorfold`
+([the license text](LICENSES/glm53f-afd-LICENSE.tensorfold.txt)). Its TP split of every expert by intermediate channel
+follows glmrt by T.J. Purtell (@wrldsuksgo2mars, [github.com/tpurtell](https://github.com/tpurtell)), a design that
+glm53f-afd reused with no code copied. Its once-a-row rotation (`rotrows_kernel` and `gateup_big`'s rotated-row copy)
+and its group order (`order_kernel`) were reimplemented for glm53f-afd, with no code copied, from MiaAI-Lab's
+[GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 2x DGX Spark recipe](https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold/tree/1576746)
+patches 0009-glm-prefill-kernels (ROWROT/SHX) and 0020-glm-prompt-experts-order (Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2026
+MiaAI-Lab); the port takes that rotation for a layer whose experts share one gate/up `suh` by the recipe's own test
+(`shared_suh`, ported unchanged in `cuda/exl3/experts.py`). The kernels are glm53f-afd at 91db3cc at its two-rank
+width (1,024 channels a rank, glm53f-rank's `G53R_WID`) with its row rotation and group order, as two evaluation
+patches of glm53f-afd build them; the reference source the GPU test pins (`tests/cuda/test_glm_g53_kernel.py`) is that
+build's `exl3_rank.cu`.
+
+The port changes data movement only; every product, sum, rounding and its order is glm53f-rank's (built with its
+`--fmad=false --ftz=false --prec-div=true`): the kernels read this node's resident TP2 half (each expert's gate, up and
+down trellis through the layer's pointer tables, and the stacked `suh`/`svh` vectors) in place of glm53f-rank's layer
+image, so no weight is copied; they take the node's BF16 rows (any row stride) in place of FP8 E4M3 rows with UE8M0
+scales (a BF16 value is widened to FP32 where glm53f-rank widens an E4M3 code and multiplies its scale; the rest of the
+rotation is theirs); the routes are the node's `pick`/`wts` rows (the 8 routed slots); the output is the half's FP32
+rows (glm53f-rank's `g53r_ffn_f32`); there is no host staging or sync, and an invalid route (glm53f-rank's fault)
+empties the plan as there and fills the call's rows with NaN; only the large-M kernels at the two-rank width are
+ported (the decode-size split kernels, the gate/up rotation warps and the dependent launch are not). `TF_GLM_EXPERT_KERNEL`
+is unset by default: the expert node then runs every call as before. Set to `g53`, the node's prompt chunks
+(`MODE_CHUNK`, `MODE_SLICE` and `MODE_PAIR` forwards) of at least `TF_GLM_EXPERT_KERNEL_ROWS` rows (default 65,
+glm53f-rank's large-M boundary) run through these kernels, and a prompt row's routed-expert sum then has glm53f-rank's
+arithmetic (outputs class); decode windows keep TensorFold's kernels.
+
